{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wireshark/wireshark/compare/master...39a3c437378890840e201d773ba52b2cdb762bc9","html_url":"https://github.com/wireshark/wireshark/compare/master...39a3c437378890840e201d773ba52b2cdb762bc9","permalink_url":"https://github.com/wireshark/wireshark/compare/wireshark:6b5925f...wireshark:39a3c43","diff_url":"https://github.com/wireshark/wireshark/compare/master...39a3c437378890840e201d773ba52b2cdb762bc9.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/wireshark/wireshark/compare/master...39a3c437378890840e201d773ba52b2cdb762bc9.patch","base_commit":{"sha":"6b5925f9aa382adae54f5d7c1832969c15669705","node_id":"C_kwDOAUV2jtoAKDZiNTkyNWY5YWEzODJhZGFlNTRmNWQ3YzE4MzI5NjljMTU2Njk3MDU","commit":{"author":{"name":"John Thacker","email":"johnthacker@gmail.com","date":"2026-11-12T21:48:39Z"},"committer":{"name":"John Thacker","email":"johnthacker@gmail.com","date":"2026-11-12T22:40:41Z"},"message":"Workaround LLVM/Clang < 20 __builtin_mul_overflow bug\n\nOn LLVM before 20, on certain platforms, when multiplication overflow is\nchecked for in a way where the width and signedness of the operands\nmeans that a signed 65-bit result is called for, Clang ends up\nrequesting the compiler-rt builtin __muloti4, which is not available in\nlibgcc. There are several shortcuts where there's no problem:\n * operands and result are all the same sign\n * both operands are unsigned and the result is signed, all same width\n * one operand signed, one unsigned, wider operand at least as wide as\n   result. result can be signed or unsigned\n\nCases which don't work (assuming one type 64-bit or larger):\n * both operands unsigned, result signed, widths not all equal\n * both operands signed, result unsigned\n * signed __int128 multiplication\n\nIn the SCSI SBC case, cast the block_size from a uint32_t to a uint64_t\nwhen doing the ckd_mul in order to hit the shortcut and avoid the bug.\n\nIn get_mem_info, memsize should just be a uint64_t, so do that. Linux\nsysinfo has unsigned longs as the operand, Windows has a DWORDLONG,\nand Apple's hw.memsize sysctl is in all practical terms a uint64_t\n(even if the SYSCTL_QUAD macro doesn't appear to enforce signedness,\nApple's own tools use it that way and negative doesn't make sense.)\n\nFix #21744\n\nThis might be easy to accidentally re-introduce, though, if we don't\ntest for this case.\n\nhttps://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/issues/16778\nhttps://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/commit/dad9e4a1657b74bc351c1e98ce4774f32fdc77fc","tree":{"sha":"5a9f0a6abbd29fb874d6cddf582ef8833418ba0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wireshark/wireshark/git/trees/5a9f0a6abbd29fb874d6cddf582ef8833418ba0a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wireshark/wireshark/git/commits/6b5925f9aa382adae54f5d7c1832969c15669705","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wireshark/wireshark/commits/6b5925f9aa382adae54f5d7c1832969c15669705","html_url":"https://github.com/wireshark/wireshark/commit/6b5925f9aa382adae54f5d7c1832969c15669705","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wireshark/wireshark/commits/6b5925f9aa382adae54f5d7c1832969c15669705/comments","author":{"login":"johnthacker","id":17785741,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3Nzg1NzQx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17785741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker","html_url":"https://github.com/johnthacker","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"johnthacker","id":17785741,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3Nzg1NzQx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17785741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker","html_url":"https://github.com/johnthacker","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a6e7df9504501eb659e50e0cf501baecf0cd3c50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wireshark/wireshark/commits/a6e7df9504501eb659e50e0cf501baecf0cd3c50","html_url":"https://github.com/wireshark/wireshark/commit/a6e7df9504501eb659e50e0cf501baecf0cd3c50"}]},"merge_base_commit":{"sha":"39a3c437378890840e201d773ba52b2cdb762bc9","node_id":"C_kwDOAUV2jtoAKDM5YTNjNDM3Mzc4ODkwODQwZTIwMWQ3NzNiYTUyYjJjZGI3NjJiYzk","commit":{"author":{"name":"John Thacker","email":"johnthacker@gmail.com","date":"2026-07-05T00:28:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"AndersBroman","email":"a.broman58@gmail.com","date":"2026-07-05T05:16:17Z"},"message":"TLS: Only copy extensions from a \"ech_outer_extensions\" extension\n\nOtherwise, as detailed in RFC 9849, this can lead to a buffer\noverrun via a packet amplification attack.\n\nhttps://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9849.html#section-5.1\nhttps://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9849.html#decompression-amp\n\nThanks to Claude and Ada Logics for the report.\n\nFix #21390","tree":{"sha":"0c3bfe7c04bb65b17fe67da3fb0931c8b4318908","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wireshark/wireshark/git/trees/0c3bfe7c04bb65b17fe67da3fb0931c8b4318908"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wireshark/wireshark/git/commits/39a3c437378890840e201d773ba52b2cdb762bc9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wireshark/wireshark/commits/39a3c437378890840e201d773ba52b2cdb762bc9","html_url":"https://github.com/wireshark/wireshark/commit/39a3c437378890840e201d773ba52b2cdb762bc9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wireshark/wireshark/commits/39a3c437378890840e201d773ba52b2cdb762bc9/comments","author":{"login":"johnthacker","id":17785741,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3Nzg1NzQx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17785741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker","html_url":"https://github.com/johnthacker","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johnthacker/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"AndersBroman","id":46320247,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MzIwMjQ3","avatar_url":"